        "original_id": "a94708de-69b5-5d55-9eec-9a8196e62282",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: Midnight Oil, Switchfoot\n- People: Peter Garrett, Jon Foreman, Tim Foreman, Chad Butler, Jerome Fontamillas, Drew Shirley\n- Songs: \"Beds Are Burning\"\n- Albums: \"Diesel and Dust\"\n- Places: Sydney, San Diego, California\n- Topics: band formation, band membership\n\nFacts:\n- By late 1976, Peter Garrett moved to Sydney to complete his law degree, and the band Farm changed its name to Midnight Oil by drawing the name from a hat.\n- Switchfoot is an American alternative rock band from San Diego, California.\n- In Switchfoot, Jon Foreman is lead vocalist and guitarist, Tim Foreman is bassist and backing vocalist, Chad Butler is drummer and percussionist, Jerome Fontamillas is guitarist, keyboardist, and backing vocalist, and Drew Shirley is guitarist and backing vocalist.\n- \"Beds Are Burning\" is a 1987 song by Midnight Oil and the first track on the album \"Diesel and Dust\".",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
